      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeha I know that with current implementation it is guarateed to be non-NULL. However as mentioned in https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/kernel/common/+/4087795/comment/8f31cc7c_bf583de1/ this internal implementation could potentially (but unlikely) change.\n\nBut yeah - after rethinking I agree: thanks to how `pkvm_panic` is implemented and used also for exception handling such as null pointer deference in (aosp/4032091 and aosp/4032093), which should prevent operating in undefined state + log this error and reset, we will catch this potential issue anyway. So probably yeah: better to not complicate this code.\n\nBTW I also realized that similarly `for_each_pkvm_initialized_cpu` doesn\u0027t check for `host_vcpus` being null (aosp/4022841) and it is also initialized same way as pcpus in `vmx_pkvm_init`",
